        "v": 5,
        "title": "Anthropic tool calling integration",
        "summary": "Implemented native Anthropic tool calling in `claude.ts` and `prompts.ts` to replace manual text parsing. The `promptClaudeStream` generator now yields `ToolCall` objects, enabling structured file reading via a `read_files` tool. `websocket-action.ts` propagates these calls to the client, where `src/index.ts` executes them and feeds results back into the message history.",
        "significance": "major",
        "at": "2026-09-15T21:05:35.489Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you use the coding assistant, it can now ask to read files by name instead of you needing to paste their contents first. Behind the scenes, the assistant now uses a structured conversation with the file system rather than scanning text, so when you open a project it can pull up specific files directly and show you their contents. You won't see a new button or setting, but you may notice the assistant handling your questions about code more smoothly without you needing to supply file contents.",
